{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>You shall increase its purchase price.</b> You shall buy for more than what the land would have been worth as a yearly rental, for indeed, when you buy for many years until the Jubilee, you will be able to use it for many years for sheepfolds, dovecotes, and the like, besides the produce." "<b>You shall diminish its purchase price.</b> That you not buy according to the reckoning of what you would have paid as a tenant — and there is no need to say, when buying for few years. And the reason: <b>for according to the number of harvests he is selling to you.</b> For when you buy for few years, you will not be able to use it for anything but the produce alone, and not for anything that cools the land such that it will not return to its vigor when you return the field to its owners — as they said, of blessed memory (Bava Metzia 109a): one who leases a field from his fellow for few years must not sow it with flax."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:56.975533772Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}